# pxx.skip — known-fail list for tools/run_fgl_corpus.sh (Pascal corpus rung 2:
# real FPC 3.2.2 fgl.pp). One driver per line: "name.pas<TAB>reason".
# Every entry MUST reference its backlog ticket. Anything failing and NOT listed
# here is a regression and reds the rung. Remove the line when the ticket is
# fixed — the runner then enforces the pass.
#
# Baseline 2026-08-25 (pxx VERSION 374): 3 pass / 4 known-fail of 7 drivers.
# 2026-08-26: 6 pass / 1 known-fail. objectlist.pas passes (inherited default
# parameters fixed); list_str and map_str pass (String-typecast in rvalue position,
# then cast-as-lvalue for builtin type names). ifclist.pas now COMPILES -- its
# `Pointer(Dest^) := Pointer(Src^)` wall is gone -- and fails one layer deeper at
# RUNTIME, on the ticket its entry now names.
# All seven build and run correctly under FPC 3.2.2, which is where the
# .expected files come from — so every entry below is a pxx gap, never a bad
# driver.
ifclist.pas	gap: compiles now; `l.Add(TFoo.Create(3))` binds the HIDDEN inherited TFPSList.Add(Pointer) instead of TFPGList.Add(const Item: T), storing the object's VMT word -- pxx does not implement method hiding. bug-p-a-descendant-method-does-not-hide-the-inherited-one
